-------------------------------------------
Virtual Jaguar v2.1.3 Rx Qt release INSTALL
-------------------------------------------


REQUIREMENTS
------------

The minimum requirements for compiling Virtual Jaguar Rx from source are:

 o  CMake
 o  GCC v4.4.x or higher
 o  libdwarf 20210528
 o  libelf 0.8.13
 o  OpenGL
 o  Qt5 5.12.0 or higher
 o  SDL2 2.30.9
 o  zlib v1.3.1 or higher

The optional requirements are:

 o  gdbstub (gdb remote access support)
 o  libcdio v0.90 or higher (Jaguar CD support)
 o  lua 5.3 or higher (future use with Tracy profiler)
 o  Tracy Profiler 0.13.x or higher (profiling support) 
 
 
PLATFORMS
--------- 

Supported O/S (WIN64 through MSYS2/MinGW64, Windows 64 bits, Linux and cygwin64).
Previously supported O/S (BeOS, FreeBSD and WIN32 through MinGW, MacOS) could work too but the CMakeLists may need modifications.


COMPILING
---------

To generate makefiles and projects, a CMakeLists file is provided.

These environement variables are supported with CMake and can be used in case of CMake cannot found the packages.
DWARFDIR, GDBSTUBDIR, LIBELFDIR, LUADIR, SDL2DIR, TRACYPROFILERDIR, LIBTRACY_PUBLIC_DIR, ZLIBDIR, QTDIR
-D<DIR>=<Path>

These options are supported with CMake, by default the LIBDWARF_ENABLE & LIBELF_ENABLE are ON.
GDBSTUB_ENABLE, LIBCDIO_ENABLE, LIBDWARF_ENABLE, LIBELF_ENABLE, TRACY_ENABLE, LUA_ENABLE
-D<Option>=ON|OFF

These options will affect the makefile.
CMAKE_VERBOSE_MAKEFILE=OFF|ON
CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=<installation path>

mkdir build
cd build
cmake -G <Generator> ..
cmake --build . --config Release


VISUAL STUDIO 2022
------------------

Beside the CMakeLists.txt file, a Win-VS2022 sub-directory contains the project and solution file.
You may have to adapt such files to handle your own development environment, usually to put the right include and library paths will be enough..
The project uses the environment variables described in the compiling section.
It can create a Debug or Release executable, and will also need the necessary DLLs in the executable directory.


SUPPORT
-------
For additional info, go to https://github.com/djipi/Virtual-Jaguar-Rx/wiki.
